      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): preserve current session aliases",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSession tools can resolve a supported display alias such as `main` to the same logical session as the requester, but the visibility guard only recognizes the exact requester key or literal `current`. Under `self` or `tree` visibility, that mismatch incorrectly rejects the current session after resolution.\n\n## Summary\n\n- preserve normalized main/current aliases in the session-tool requester context\n- treat those aliases as the same requester session under `self` and `tree` visibility\n- pass the alias set through `sessions_list`, `sessions_history`, and `sessions_send`\n\nThis keeps current-session access working when a caller and the session resolver use different supported aliases for the same main session, without broadening visibility to unrelated same-agent sessions.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/agents/tools/sessions-access.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.agents-tools.config.ts` — 1 file passed, 30 tests passed\n- `pnpm format:check -- src/agents/tools/sessions-access.test.ts src/agents/tools/sessions-access.ts src/agents/tools/sessions-history-tool.ts src/agents/tools/sessions-list-tool.ts src/agents/tools/sessions-send-tool.ts src/plugin-sdk/session-visibility.ts` — passed\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` — passed\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` — clean\n\nBehavior addressed: current-session main aliases were rejected by `self`/`tree` visibility after canonical session resolution.\n\nReal environment tested: local OpenClaw source checkout on macOS with Node 24 and the repository Vitest/tsgo wrappers.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/agents/tools/sessions-access.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.agents-tools.config.ts`\n\nEvidence after fix: the focused suite passes 30/30 tests, including alias access under both `self` and `tree` visibility while an unrelated direct session remains forbidden.\n\nObserved result after fix: configured aliases of the requester are accepted as the current session; unrelated same-agent sessions retain the existing visibility error.\n\nWhat was not tested: a deployed cron-to-channel round trip; deployment and live channel credentials were intentionally unchanged.\n",
        "branch": "fix/cron-telegram-current-history-v2",
